// Icon geometry for `AppIcon`, transcribed **verbatim** from the SVGs the Vue
// renders (`src/assets/icons/*.svg`): the path data, the view box and the
// stroke width are that file's own, character for character, with its `<path>`
// elements split into the stroked ones and the filled ones so that `AppIcon`
// can layer them. Several icons are both, which is why the two lists are
// separate.
//
// The icon set is Font Awesome Free and Ionicons; the two brand marks
// (`modrinth`, `curseforge`) are the SVGs under `src/assets/images/`, inlined
// here as path data so that `AppIcon` can tint them.
//
// An icon is described by up to four lookups:
//   * `stroke-commands` — outline sub-paths (drawn with `stroke`);
//   * `fill-commands`   — solid sub-paths (drawn with `fill`);
//   * `viewbox`         — square view box edge (24, 32, 512, 593 or 640);
//   * `stroke-width`    — stroke width in view box units (0 when the icon has
//                         no stroked sub-path).
export global Icons {
